WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.780
How can a neuron cut off a branch with enzymes that could kill the whole cell?

2
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.640
Pruning means removing an axon branch from a neuron that survives.

3
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.520
The enzymes are caspases.

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.640
Caspases are proteases that dismantle a cell during apoptosis.

5
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.620
Yet a neuron can use them on one axon and live.

6
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.640
Mouse sympathetic neurons show how.

7
00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:33.083
Researchers built a chamber with two compartments.

8
00:00:33.803 --> 00:00:38.083
The cell bodies of mouse sympathetic neurons sat in one compartment.

9
00:00:38.923 --> 00:00:42.143
Their axons grew through narrow grooves into the other.

10
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:47.303
Many sympathetic neurons send branches toward targets that make NGF.

11
00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:53.603
Both sides held NGF, a trophic factor, which is a growth factor supplied by the

12
00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:58.243
target. This setup lets them remove NGF from the axons alone.

13
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:02.897
First, remove NGF from the axons alone.

14
00:01:03.717 --> 00:01:05.137
The axons degenerate.

15
00:01:05.697 --> 00:01:08.957
The cell bodies live, because they still have NGF.

16
00:01:09.797 --> 00:01:11.237
This is the local route.

17
00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:18.557
This pruning needs three caspases: caspase-9, caspase-3, and caspase-6.

18
00:01:19.397 --> 00:01:21.577
It does not need Apaf-1.

19
00:01:21.577 --> 00:01:23.217
Keep that name in mind.

20
00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:28.427
Now start again, and remove NGF from the whole dish.

21
00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:30.947
This time the neurons die.

22
00:01:31.707 --> 00:01:33.327
This is the whole-cell route.

23
00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.967
Their death needs Apaf-1.

24
00:01:36.687 --> 00:01:39.167
Apaf-1 builds the apoptosome.

25
00:01:39.827 --> 00:01:44.467
The apoptosome is the usual activator of caspase-9 in apoptosis.

26
00:01:45.327 --> 00:01:52.267
When NGF is removed from the whole dish, loss of caspase-6 no longer protects the axons.

27
00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.527
Now test the idea.

28
00:01:55.427 --> 00:01:58.087
Take Apaf-1 away from the neurons.

29
00:01:58.887 --> 00:02:01.467
Remove NGF from the axons alone.

30
00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:05.887
The axons still degenerate, and the cell bodies live.

31
00:02:07.087 --> 00:02:09.587
Now remove NGF from the whole dish.

32
00:02:10.507 --> 00:02:12.387
These neurons resist death.

33
00:02:13.347 --> 00:02:16.567
Without Apaf-1, the whole-cell route is blocked.

34
00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:21.547
The whole-cell route needs Apaf-1 to activate caspase-9.

35
00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:28.250
The same caspases can be reached by two routes, one local and one global.

36
00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:34.770
The local route uses caspase-9, -3 and -6, but not Apaf-1.

37
00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.310
The whole-cell route needs the apoptosome.

38
00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.250
The routes share enzymes but are wired differently.

39
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:45.710
So a neuron can lose one branch and live.

40
00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.230
Remember: only the whole-cell route needs Apaf-1.
